nss_init: allow triggering the coredump without the debug sysctl

The manual coredump trigger (sysctl dev.nss.general.coredump=1) is gated
on nss_ctl_debug, but the sysctl that sets that flag is compiled out in
this build, so the trigger can never fire.  The trigger is the only way
to get the firmware's internal log ring dumped (patch 0108) after the
wifili start wedges the phys_if node on IPQ5018 - the firmware is not
crashed, so the firmware-initiated coredump path never runs.

Drop the gate; writing 1 to the sysctl is already an explicit root-only
action.

--- a/nss_init.c
+++ b/nss_init.c
@@ -403,7 +403,7 @@ static int nss_coredump_handler(compat_const struct ctl_table *ctl, int write, v
 		 * when NSS FW crashes, so OEM/ODM have a chance to use mdump
 		 * to dump crash dump (coredump) and send dump to us for analysis.
 		 */
-		if ((write) && (nss_ctl_debug != 0) && nss_cmd_buf.coredump == 1) {
+		if ((write) && nss_cmd_buf.coredump == 1) {
 			printk("Coredumping to DDR\n");
 			nss_hal_send_interrupt(nss_ctx, NSS_H2N_INTR_TRIGGER_COREDUMP);
 		}
